// The compiler-bundled collections prelude: the library collections that language syntax binds to by closed
// `@compiler_role` roles (decision 0026). It is always loaded, separately from the concurrency and role preludes,
// so a caller-supplied concurrency prelude never removes it, and it is a runtime unit (it may declare C bindings
// to the runtime's collection functions).
//
// It is empty until the library `Array<T>` replaces the builtin array: this file only reserves the third prelude,
// its source identity and its packaging.
